{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"A partial return uses the **original order prices and discount**, counting only the quantities returned. In [calculateRefund](/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/scrubjay-example/src/returns.ts:18):\n\n```text\nsubtotal = sum(original unit price in cents × returned quantity)\nrefund   = Math.round(subtotal × (1 − discountPercent / 100))\n```\n\nRounding happens once, after summing all returned items. For example, returning one item priced at 2,000¢ with a 10% order discount refunds **1,800¢**.\n\nAll 7 return tests pass; I didn’t run the full suite.\nKnown rounding issue: floating-point arithmetic can under-refund by 1¢—1,990¢ at 55% off refunds 895¢, while the order charges 896¢."}}
